[/tikz]

A rectangle has width $w$ centimetres. Its area $A$ square centimetres is modelled by $A=w^{2}+2w$.
(a) Use the graph to find the width when the area is $48$ cm$^{2}$, then calculate the rectangle's perimeter.
(b) Use the equation to calculate the area when $w=4$, and find how much smaller it is than $48$ cm$^{2}$.
(c) Explain why negative widths are excluded.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{modelblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=6cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={black,->},xmin=0,xmax=7,ymin=0,ymax=60,xtick={0,1,...,7},ytick={0,6,...,60},grid=major,grid style={draw=black!20},scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={$w$ (cm)},ylabel={$A$ (cm$^{2}$)}]
\addplot[modelblue,thick,domain=0:6.8,samples=101] {x*x+2*x};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

